# Implementing a new instruction (LLDAR / CLLDAR), following workflow-new-instruction.md.
# Render:   d2 --watch herd-workflow-new-instruction.d2
#           d2 --scale 2 herd-workflow-new-instruction.d2 herd-workflow-new-instruction.svg
# Links point to the diff hunk in the GitHub commit view of the fork:
#   cae6291 adds LLDAR (+ LA annotation, bob edge), 03c4483 adds CLLDAR.
# Format: commit/<sha>#diff-<sha256(path)>R<line in new file>. D2 does not
# substitute variables inside markdown, so each URL is spelled out.

vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: elk
  }
}

direction: right

classes: {
  phase: {
    grid-columns: 1
    vertical-gap: 24
    style: {
      fill: "#e8f0fe"
      stroke: "#3b6fd8"
      stroke-width: 2
      border-radius: 10
      font-size: 24
      bold: true
    }
  }
  handoff: {
    style: {
      stroke: "#3b6fd8"
      stroke-width: 2
      font-size: 14
    }
  }
}

# ───────────────────────── 1 · Instruction, parser, lexer ─────────────────────────

syntax: "1 · Create Instruction, Update Parser / Lexer" {
  class: phase

  desc: |md
    Make the litmus syntax parse into an instruction object:

    1. introduce the instruction in **AArch64Base.ml**:
       [**LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-87c59e17c30b4a451f5222d06442d112d13bc5348634c3664db613942d49cf4cR1254) reuses the LDAR struct with a new `ld_type`,
       [**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-87c59e17c30b4a451f5222d06442d112d13bc5348634c3664db613942d49cf4cR1446) gets its own constructor
    2. introduce a new annotation: limited acquire
       ([**LA**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-05772012f80903bb4d4dc5c9998c03e96d3a69e1f313be7d2e138a89bb93f4d3R19))
  |
}

# ───────────────────────── 2 · Semantics ─────────────────────────

semantics: "2 · Instruction Semantics and CAT Semantics" {
  class: phase

  desc: |md
    Give the instruction meaning, as events and as ordering:

    3. encode the instruction semantics with the monad binders
       ([**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-f2a12c2f4bc2d0aa25e415c57b77bfe6c912fb2a2b841e23fc03922cdeafb1ecR4241))
    4. introduce limited-acquire edges to the cat model
       ([**bob**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-48de46133a6939978d62812c18eb510164eab583412b943fb1674f9d2cb10452R139))
    5. write integration tests
       ([**A266**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-7e3f509470844ba0a9291375ffa0e902741549ad6a7f6dfbc671b68a4f83515aR1) for LLDAR, [**A267**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-3633e9d5635759e4e77a9a37a43f3b06cb1fb62330e06491d4a10f03a6f7e403R1) for CLLDAR)
  |
}

# ───────────────────────── 3 · Litmus tests ─────────────────────────

litmus: "3 · Write Litmus Tests to Check Intended Behaviour" {
  class: phase

  desc: |md
    For each instruction, one test that the ordering holds and one
    that it stops at a later memory access:

    6. **LLDAR**
       - ordering ([**MP+rel+LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-703014ffa7c91dda91ccc4ef42953c24668cd4d31d182f1d9590d79fa2b114c1R1))
       - no ordering past a later memory instruction
         ([**MP+rel+LLDAR-fail**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-ba6c4ce62159c99b1487bc99a0e1a5bdc6ea508e7688aa2a90975c5fda101463R1))
    7. **CLLDAR**
       - ordering ([**MP+rel+CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-e7cf9486ace110b1585c5bab8eac64c890bb98defa07d338c30b9316e70b82e9R1))
       - no ordering past a later memory instruction
         ([**MP+rel+CLLDAR-fail**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-609655c09c0f39317bb981754e9152c589defcd7ed6830a596a78ef13859f1abR1))
  |
}

# ───────────────────────── Hand-offs ─────────────────────────

syntax -> semantics {class: handoff}
semantics -> litmus {class: handoff}
